@flexiarg operator/reroute-around-the-capped-seat
@title Reroute Around the Capped Seat
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 4 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-1UIrcy turn-G1cBQ0 turn-N1UMLv turn-vOEd8P
@parent collaboration-coherence/stasis
@context Work was assigned or assumed to flow through a seat that has hit an external capacity limit (usage quota).

! conclusion: Report the cap plainly, name the substitute seat ('a fresh Kimi seat'), and reroute — the stuck axis is the seat, not the project.

  + IF:
    The seat's unavailability is a capacity cap, not a competence gap, and a substitute seat of another family has capacity.

  + HOWEVER:
    Substituting seats loses the incumbent's session context and can duplicate work; but waiting on the cap converts one seat's quota into the project's stall, and the cap's duration is outside the operator's control.

  + THEN:
    Report the cap plainly, name the substitute seat ('a fresh Kimi seat'), and reroute — the stuck axis is the seat, not the project.

  + BECAUSE:
    Stasis distinguishes a stuck axis from a stuck project and looks for the moving dimension; this candidate is that move with the axis concretised to agent seats — Codex's quota is the stuck axis, the fresh seat is the moving dimension.
